  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The protocol describes an ongoing implementation study limited to only two wards within a single municipality, meaning the portal's operational feasibility and utility have not yet been tested at scale.",
      "what": "This study protocol outlines a mixed-methods implementation project to build an integrated urban health data portal in two wards of Budhanilkantha municipality, Nepal. The researchers will conduct stakeholder interviews, policy reviews, social mapping, a door-to-door household census, and health facility assessments to generate granular, geocoded ward-level data. These primary datasets will be linked with existing routine health and administrative databases using common identifiers to feed into interactive dashboards and GIS mapping tools.",
      "why": "It establishes a proof-of-concept framework for combining routine administrative data with primary local data, enabling municipal governments in low- and middle-income countries to make spatial, equity-focused decisions that address rapid urban growth and health disparities."
    }
